# 45. Common Beginner Mistakes

## Mistake 1 — Using SUM on text

Wrong:

```sql
SELECT SUM(employee_name)
FROM employees;
```

`SUM()` is intended for numeric data.

---

## Mistake 2 — Assuming NULL means zero

These are different:

```text
NULL
0
```

`NULL` means:

> Unknown / missing / not provided.

Zero means:

> The numeric value is actually zero.

---

## Mistake 3 — Using COUNT(column) when you need row count

If you want the number of rows:

```sql
COUNT(*)
```

is generally the clearest choice.

---

## Mistake 4 — Forgetting that COUNT(column) ignores NULL

```sql
COUNT(bonus)
```

does not count employees whose bonus is `NULL`.

---

## Mistake 5 — Expecting an aggregate query to return every row

This:

```sql
SELECT AVG(salary)
FROM employees;
```

returns one summary result.

It does not return one average salary for each employee.

